# NVSHMEM IBGDA fault-injection + diagnostic test hook
#
# Target: NVSHMEM commit 7bb2e99c, src/modules/transport/ibgda/ibgda.cpp
# Default OFF: does nothing unless an env var below is set, so a normal build is
# behaviourally identical to stock NVSHMEM. Apply: git apply <this file>.
#
# NVSHMEM_IBGDA_FAULT_INJECT=local_err:<ms> | peer_err:<ms> | qp2err:<ms>
#   A detached host thread, <ms> after connect_endpoints, moves this PE's RC/DCI
#   DEVX QPs to ERR (MLX5_CMD_OP_2ERR_QP). F1 sets it on rain, F3 on sunny.
#
# NVSHMEM_IBGDA_FAULT_WATCH=<period_ms>   (diagnostic, default off)
#   A host thread that every <period_ms> issues QUERY_QP (qpc.state + SQ wqebb
#   counters) on each RC/DCI QP and QUERY_CQ (cqc producer/consumer/status) on
#   its send CQ, and dumps the 64-byte collapsed CQ slot (from GPU or host mem).
#   Used to locate where a requester error completion goes.
#
# F2a (oob within MR), F2b (invalid rkey) and F4 (proc_kill) need no library
# change: F2a/F2b are driven from the test binary, F4 by SIGKILLing the peer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
